    <string name="on_boarding_first_title" translatable="false">SwipeLauncher</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_first_desc">This is a launcher that works on swipes. Tap anywhere on the screen to bring up the menu, then, without releasing your finger, drag it to the item you need. The action specified for this element will be executed.</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_second_title">Menu</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_second_desc">You can create any number of menus. You can add any number of items to the menu, which will be arranged in a circle. All menus and their elements can be changed in the settings.</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_third_title">Types of actions</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_third_desc">1. Open app\n2. Open circle menu (opens a new menu at this location)\n3. Open settings (opens launcher settings)\n4. Call (makes a call to the specified phone number)\n5. Dial(opens the calling application with the entered phone number, all you have to do is press the button to make a call)\n6. Turn on the flashlight\n7. Turn off the flashlight\n8. Change flashlight condition (if it’s on, then turn it off and if it’s off, then turn it on)\n9. Open url</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_fourth_title">Types of images</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_fourth_desc">1. App image\n2. Default image (select from the list provided)\n3. User image (after selecting the picture is automatically saved in the application, you can delete the original)</string>
    <string name="go_to_settings">Go to settings</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_fifth_title">Apps list</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_fifth_desc">To open the list of all apps, double-tap anywhere. When you tap an app, it will open. When you tap and hold, a app info window will appear where you can delete or view detailed information about the app in the settings.</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_sixth_title">Settings</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_sixth_desc">To access the launcher settings, find and open the SwipeLauncher app in the list of all apps.\nYou can configure:\n1. All menus and their elements\n2. The action when pressing the clock (widget on the home screen)\n3. The text color on the wallpaper (the color of the clock widget) — black or white (choose so that it doesn’t blend in with the wallpaper)\n4. Opening the last app during a search — if only that app matches the search query (you can enable or disable this feature).\n5. Displaying the keyboard when opening the app list — to start searching immediately (you can enable or disable this feature).\n6. Selecting the app opening action when selecting an app icon — for faster configuration of menu items.</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_seventh_title">All circle menus</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_seventh_desc">In the list of all menus, you can add a new menu, delete an old one (delete works for all but the main one, delete by pressing and holding) or change an existing one.</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_eighth_title">Changing the circle menu</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_eighth_desc">To open the menu editing window, click on the desired menu in the list of all menus. You can change the menu name by editing the text at the top. You can also add, edit, and delete menu items. When you click on the action of the selected item, a dialog box opens, where you can change the action. The same applies to images.</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_ninth_title">Set as default launcher</string>
    <string name="on_boarding_ninth_desc">You can set SwipeLauncher as your default launcher in system settings. Your choice can always be changed in the launcher settings and in the system settings.</string>
